1
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:13,733
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:15,062 --> 00:00:18,865
Abdullah Ibn Imam Ahmad(عَبدُالله ابن اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ), Abdullah(عَبدالله); the son of Al Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ); he said;

3
00:00:19,292 --> 00:00:22,419
that he was there when his father was passing away.

4
00:00:24,059 --> 00:00:28,923
And his father was going into the Sakrah(سكرة); the state of unconsciousness.

5
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:38,135
And by the way, when you are going from Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) to Akhirah(آخرة); it's a very difficult change.

6
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:41,787
You've been in this world for 60 or 70 years.

7
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:45,034
And now, you are going through a completely different world.

8
00:00:45,747 --> 00:00:50,059
So that change between these two stages is difficult.

9
00:00:50,639 --> 00:00:53,106
And sometimes it doesn't happen immediately.

10
00:00:53,126 --> 00:00:57,261
So you'll find the person, is going back and forth in this stage of Sakrah(سكرة).

11
00:00:57,908 --> 00:01:01,714
To simplify the explanation of this; think about sleep.

12
00:01:01,781 --> 00:01:03,876
Because sleep is the minor death.

13
00:01:04,576 --> 00:01:05,510
اَلْوَفَاةُ الصُّغْرَى

14
00:01:05,923 --> 00:01:06,230
Sleep!

15
00:01:06,296 --> 00:01:09,095
وٱلَّذِى يَتَوَفَّىٰكُم حینا منامکم

16
00:01:09,228 --> 00:01:13,094
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And He Is the One, Who takes your souls when you are sleeping.

17
00:01:13,301 --> 00:01:14,988
Sleep is a minor death.

18
00:01:15,674 --> 00:01:19,196
When you are awake, and you're going to the different stage of sleep.

19
00:01:19,443 --> 00:01:22,470
You go through interface between these two.

20
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:25,056
So you are not asleep, and you're not awake.

21
00:01:25,656 --> 00:01:27,850
And then you enter into the stage of sleep.

22
00:01:28,923 --> 00:01:34,985
So you're going from awakening to sleeping, and you're going through this interface between the two.

23
00:01:35,905 --> 00:01:38,152
The same thing happens before death.

24
00:01:38,770 --> 00:01:43,382
You are going through this interface between the two stages of life and death.

25
00:01:43,856 --> 00:01:49,969
So there is moments in which you are on the other side of the world, and moments in which you are in this side of the world.

26
00:01:50,349 --> 00:01:55,701
Abdullah Ibn Imam Ahmad(عَبدُالله ابن اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) says that, his father went into the stage of unconsciousness.

27
00:01:55,994 --> 00:01:57,841
And then his father started saying;

28
00:01:57,861 --> 00:01:59,718
لَا بَعَدْ، لَا بَعَدْ

29
00:01:59,961 --> 00:02:01,416
No; not yet!

30
00:02:01,570 --> 00:02:02,770
No; not yet!

31
00:02:04,183 --> 00:02:05,640
Abdullah(عَبدالله) was worried.

32
00:02:06,650 --> 00:02:10,046
Imagine! You hear your father saying; No; not yet! No; not yet!

33
00:02:10,093 --> 00:02:11,773
What would you interpret it to mean?

34
00:02:12,786 --> 00:02:14,425
What would you think, it means?

35
00:02:15,035 --> 00:02:16,956
I don't want to die yet, right.

36
00:02:17,342 --> 00:02:19,056
No; not yet! No; not yet!

37
00:02:19,482 --> 00:02:23,606
You would interpret it as meaning; I do not want to die yet.

38
00:02:24,594 --> 00:02:26,208
So Abdullah(عَبدالله) was very concerned.

39
00:02:27,381 --> 00:02:31,026
So he asked his father; Oh my father! When his father woke up;

40
00:02:31,566 --> 00:02:35,640
Oh my father! Why were you saying; Not yet! Not yet!

41
00:02:36,446 --> 00:02:38,002
Al-Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) said;

42
00:02:38,482 --> 00:02:43,710
إن الشيطان قائم بحذائي عاضٌّ على أنامله

43
00:02:43,856 --> 00:02:46,903
 يقول: يا أحمد فتّني، يا أحمد فتّني،

44
00:02:47,323 --> 00:02:50,818
فكنت أقول له: لا بعد، لا بعد، حتى أموت

45
00:02:52,354 --> 00:02:53,567
Al-Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) said;

46
00:02:53,854 --> 00:02:59,089
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) was standing right next to me; biting on his fingers and saying;

47
00:02:59,109 --> 00:03:01,749
Oh Ahmad(اَحْمَدْ)! You have slipped out of my hands.

48
00:03:01,782 --> 00:03:04,276
Oh Ahmad(اَحْمَدْ)! You have slipped out of my hands.

49
00:03:04,604 --> 00:03:08,136
So I was telling him; No, not yet! Not yet! until I die.

50
00:03:08,618 --> 00:03:10,925
The battle between me and you is still happening.

51
00:03:11,052 --> 00:03:13,613
Not until I die; will I be saved from you.

52
00:03:13,993 --> 00:03:18,839
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) was biting his fingers; upset because he lost Al Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

53
00:03:19,106 --> 00:03:21,006
Because Al Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) is slipping from his hands.

54
00:03:21,312 --> 00:03:22,702
So Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) was so angry and upset.

55
00:03:22,722 --> 00:03:24,742
He was biting his fingers and saying;

56
00:03:24,762 --> 00:03:26,754
Ahmad(اَحْمَدْ), you have slipped away from my hands.

57
00:03:27,028 --> 00:03:29,528
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) said; Not yet; until I die.

58
00:03:30,968 --> 00:03:37,260
Look at the believer! How he keeps on fighting until the last moment.

59
00:03:37,573 --> 00:03:38,844
We never give up!

60
00:03:41,364 --> 00:03:44,906
If we are proud; we would say, Yes! I won against you.

61
00:03:45,793 --> 00:03:47,853
But Al Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) is saying; No, until I die.

62
00:03:48,846 --> 00:03:54,326
So this could happen and if it could happen; is something extremely dangerous.

63
00:03:55,279 --> 00:03:58,078
Imam Ibn Taymiyah(امام اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه); Shaikh-al-Islam(شيخ الاسلام), Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه); he says;

64
00:03:58,164 --> 00:04:02,998
The reason, why this happens is, because Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) realizes that, this is his last chance with you.

65
00:04:03,364 --> 00:04:05,227
If he misses it; you're gone.

66
00:04:05,993 --> 00:04:09,753
If he misses you in the last moment, he missed you.

67
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:17,980
That is why, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) emphasizes and gives special attention to the last moments of your life.

68
00:04:19,526 --> 00:04:27,269
So put the criteria to yourself and think about it; if you are losing to Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) now, when the battle is easy.

69
00:04:28,035 --> 00:04:30,842
What would happen to you in the last moments, where it gets tough?

70
00:04:32,058 --> 00:04:37,145
If you are already losing the battle now; when Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is giving you a half of his attention.

71
00:04:37,558 --> 00:04:41,605
What will happen when he gives you his complete attention; when he devotes his efforts for you?

72
00:04:42,671 --> 00:04:45,541
These are the Fitan(فِتَنْ). And that's why, we say in our Salah(صلوة);

73
00:04:45,568 --> 00:04:48,541
اللهم إنا نعوذ بك من فتنة المحيا والممات

74
00:04:49,074 --> 00:04:51,771
We seek refuge in You from the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of life and death.

75
00:04:51,864 --> 00:04:53,064
This is the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of death.

76
00:04:54,504 --> 00:04:58,610
Let's talk about Asbab Su'al Khatimah(اَسْبَابْ سُوءَالْخَاتِمَه); the reasons for evil ending.

77
00:04:59,363 --> 00:05:03,360
Because the most important stage of your life is Al-Khawateem(خواتيم); the ending.

78
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,000
من مات على شيء بعث عليه

79
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:08,646
Whoever dies in something will be resurrected on it.

80
00:05:09,093 --> 00:05:12,476
If you died in Hajj(حَجْ) with Ihram(احرام), making Talbiah(تلبيه),

81
00:05:12,543 --> 00:05:15,850
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; On the Day of Judgment, you will be resurrected saying;

82
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:17,210
لَبَّيْكَ اللَّهُمَّ لَبَّيْكَ

83
00:05:17,553 --> 00:05:19,951
And if you die as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) in the battle;

84
00:05:20,158 --> 00:05:25,814
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; On the Day of Judgment, you would come out of your grave with your injury bleeding;

85
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:28,334
just like it was bleeding when you died in the battlefield.

86
00:05:30,307 --> 00:05:32,087
من مات على شيء بعث عليه

87
00:05:32,107 --> 00:05:35,604
When you die on something; you will be resurrected on that same thing that you were doing.

88
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:39,227
That's why the most important stage of our life is Al-Khawateem(الخواتیم).

89
00:05:39,544 --> 00:05:42,699
And  that's why, Rasool Allah ﷺ used to always says in the Hadith(حديث);

90
00:05:43,293 --> 00:05:45,686
اللهمَّ اجعل خير أعمال خواتمها

91
00:05:46,126 --> 00:05:49,106
Oh Allah! Make the best of my deeds; the last deeds.

92
00:05:50,093 --> 00:05:51,639
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث);

93
00:05:51,866 --> 00:05:56,255
يعمل احدكم بعمل الجنة حتى لا يكون بينها وبين الجنت ذراع،

94
00:05:56,408 --> 00:05:59,731
فيسبق عليه الكتاب، فيعمل بعمل أهل النار فيدخل النار

95
00:06:00,524 --> 00:06:06,084
One of you; would do the deeds of the people of paradise until, the only one foot is between you and Paradise,

96
00:06:06,251 --> 00:06:11,610
and then in the end; you would do the deeds of the people of hellfire, and you would die, and you would enter into hellfire.

97
00:06:12,290 --> 00:06:18,353
All of your life; you were doing the actions of the people of Jannah(جنة), and in the end; you messed up, and then you end up in hellfire.

98
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:20,067
And the opposite could happen too.

99
00:06:20,127 --> 00:06:26,272
You could be doing the deeds of the people of hellfire, in the last moment of your life; you do something good; you die; you go to Jannah(جنة).

100
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:29,246
So the most important stage is the last stage.

101
00:06:29,646 --> 00:06:32,176
What are the reasons for evil endings?

102
00:06:32,848 --> 00:06:34,841
نسأل الله عزوجل حسن الختام

103
00:06:35,095 --> 00:06:38,222
We asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; the good, blessed ending.

104
00:06:38,755 --> 00:06:40,922
Reasons of evil ending.

105
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:41,762
Number one;

106
00:06:41,795 --> 00:06:43,388
الفساد في الاعتقاد

107
00:06:43,588 --> 00:06:46,074
Corruption and defect in the belief.

108
00:06:47,827 --> 00:06:50,227
Corruption and defect in the belief.

109
00:06:51,007 --> 00:06:53,187
Let me give you an example, an analogy.

110
00:06:55,197 --> 00:06:57,058
Let's assume; you bought a computer.

111
00:06:59,038 --> 00:07:04,601
And you started working on that computer, for the first month; it's working fine, the second month it's working fine.

112
00:07:05,231 --> 00:07:12,656
And then you put it through a rigorous application; and the computer failed and broke down.

113
00:07:14,423 --> 00:07:15,895
You take it and you see what's the problem?

114
00:07:15,915 --> 00:07:18,348
You find that there was a defect from day one.

115
00:07:18,728 --> 00:07:22,410
But this defect did not show from day one, because you were treating it gently.

116
00:07:22,850 --> 00:07:25,777
You were using the computer for easy and simple applications.

117
00:07:26,203 --> 00:07:33,150
But when you put it through the rigorous test; a serious application; a serious program; it broke down.

118
00:07:33,457 --> 00:07:34,143
Why?

119
00:07:34,163 --> 00:07:35,474
Because there was a hidden defect.

120
00:07:35,827 --> 00:07:37,807
This defect didn't show up on day one.

121
00:07:37,867 --> 00:07:39,141
It didn't show up on day two.

122
00:07:39,261 --> 00:07:40,904
It grew up fine for two months.

123
00:07:41,157 --> 00:07:43,417
But when things became tough; it broke down.

124
00:07:44,471 --> 00:07:46,913
Because, there was a hidden defect; You didn't see it.

125
00:07:47,107 --> 00:07:49,973
You thought that the computer is brand new, and nothing is wrong with it.

126
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,467
But there was something hidden.

127
00:07:53,357 --> 00:07:58,629
So you could be living now, thinking that your Eeman(ايمان) is perfect, and your Aqeedah(عَقِيدة) is fine.

128
00:07:59,289 --> 00:08:02,268
You have a Bid'ah(بدعة) or an innovation or doubts.

129
00:08:02,308 --> 00:08:07,858
You have doubts in Qur'an; doubts about the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); doubts about the laws of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

130
00:08:07,878 --> 00:08:11,091
You have some doubts hidden somewhere in the corner; in the heart.

131
00:08:14,205 --> 00:08:18,801
And then death approaches, and Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) puts you through the test.

132
00:08:18,927 --> 00:08:21,291
Things become difficult on you in those last moments.

133
00:08:22,504 --> 00:08:27,448
And that fallacy, that problem, that defect, shows up.

134
00:08:28,555 --> 00:08:31,041
You find out that there was a corruption in your belief.

135
00:08:32,541 --> 00:08:35,907
When you find out there's a corruption in your belief; you what do you do?

136
00:08:35,987 --> 00:08:37,527
You give up your whole belief.

137
00:08:39,134 --> 00:08:44,401
Because you discover there's something wrong with it; You think there's something wrong with Islam, and you would give up the whole thing,

138
00:08:44,947 --> 00:08:46,614
and you would lose it all.

139
00:08:47,194 --> 00:08:51,408
Just like the computer, a problem happens with it nowadays; you throw the computer; you don't go and fix it.

140
00:08:52,188 --> 00:08:55,661
So you can throw the whole thing; and you lose the whole battle.

141
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,120
And that's why, Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبنِ ألقَيِّم) says;

142
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:07,239
We don't expect that Allahسُبحانه وتعالى would mislead anyone, who was on the straight path; except if that person had a hidden defect.

143
00:09:07,739 --> 00:09:15,922
He said; We believe that, out of the Mercy of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; Allah would not mislead anyone, if that person was true righteous.

144
00:09:16,468 --> 00:09:22,156
There must be something wrong, and that defect showed up in one moment of time.

145
00:09:23,310 --> 00:09:24,336
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

146
00:09:24,443 --> 00:09:29,766
قل ھل ننبِّئُكُم بِالْأَخْسَرِينَ أَعْمَالًا۝

147
00:09:30,095 --> 00:09:40,311
الَّذِينَ ضَلَّ سَعْيُهُمْ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَهُمْ يَحْسَبُونَ أَنَّهُمْ يُحْسِنُوننَ صُنْعًا۝

148
00:09:41,458 --> 00:09:47,678
Allah says; Say! Shall We tell you the greatest losers in respect to their deeds?

149
00:09:47,965 --> 00:09:55,787
They are those, whom efforts have been wasted in this life, while they thought they were acquiring good by their deeds.

150
00:09:56,747 --> 00:09:58,833
Allah Is telling us about the biggest losers.

151
00:09:59,073 --> 00:10:03,220
They are the ones who are thinking; they're doing well; but they're doing wrong.

152
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:08,932
You find that somebody is very righteous, very righteous; but he is doing it the wrong way.

153
00:10:08,952 --> 00:10:11,005
He's not following the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

154
00:10:11,292 --> 00:10:12,767
It's all unaccepted.

155
00:10:16,387 --> 00:10:18,940
Second reason for Su'al Khatimah(سُوءَالْخَاتِمَه);

156
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:21,160
العدول عن الاستقامة

157
00:10:21,967 --> 00:10:24,459
Diversion from the straight path.

158
00:10:26,492 --> 00:10:30,812
A person could be on the straight path, and then he decides to divert.

159
00:10:31,432 --> 00:10:38,256
When he takes that short cut, or short turn, what happens is; it's like a fork.

160
00:10:38,603 --> 00:10:44,003
It starts out with a small angle, but then it gets further and further and further away.

161
00:10:44,405 --> 00:10:48,218
The turn in the beginning seems very small; the angle is very small.

162
00:10:48,378 --> 00:10:52,334
But the further you go; the more further apart you become.

163
00:10:53,861 --> 00:11:00,774
Iblees(اِبْلِيس); Ar-Rajeem(الرَّجِيْم); he was one of the righteous, but he did that small mistake.

164
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:09,347
He did that small mistake out of a great problem, which is Kibr(كبر); arrogance.

165
00:11:10,974 --> 00:11:15,343
And he became the worst of the creation; Bal'aam(بلعام).

166
00:11:15,689 --> 00:11:16,896
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

167
00:11:16,949 --> 00:11:25,580
وَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَأَ الَّذِي آتَيْنَاهُ آيَاتِنَا فَانسَلَخَ مِنْهَا

168
00:11:26,031 --> 00:11:33,513
 فَانسَلَخَ مِنْهَا فَأَتْبَعَهُ الشَّيْطَانُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْغَاوِينَ۝

169
00:11:33,947 --> 00:11:44,579
وَلَوْ شِئْنَا لَرَفَعْنَاهُ بِهَا وَلَٰكِنَّهُ أَخْلَدَ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ وَاتَّبَعَ هَوَاهُ ۚ

170
00:11:44,879 --> 00:11:52,583
فَمَثَلُهُ كَمَثَلِ الْكَلْبِ إِن تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْهِ يَلْهَثثْ أَوْ تَتْرُكْهُ يَلْهَث ۚ

171
00:11:52,917 --> 00:12:05,632
ذَّٰلِكَ مَثَلُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوا بِآيَاتِنَا ۚ فَاقْصُصِ الْقَصَصَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ۝

172
00:12:06,252 --> 00:12:13,635
Allah says; And recite to them the story of him, to whom We gave our Ayaat(آيات), but he threw them away.

173
00:12:14,115 --> 00:12:23,301
So Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) followed him up, and he became of those who went astray, and hell We built, We would surely Have elevated him therewith,

174
00:12:23,601 --> 00:12:27,488
but he clung to the earth and followed his own vain desires.

175
00:12:28,714 --> 00:12:32,428
This Ayah(آية) is talking about someone who received the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah,

176
00:12:33,697 --> 00:12:35,224
received the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah,

177
00:12:36,155 --> 00:12:42,163
and then he detached himself from the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah, and followed his own desires.

178
00:12:42,823 --> 00:12:46,765
So Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) followed up, and he was misled and misguided.

179
00:12:46,785 --> 00:12:47,499
Why?

180
00:12:47,812 --> 00:12:49,026
أَخْلَدَ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ

181
00:12:49,199 --> 00:12:51,521
Because he was clung and attached to this world.

182
00:12:51,574 --> 00:12:52,994
Look at what this world could do.

183
00:12:53,154 --> 00:12:58,824
This is a person who had the knowledge and had the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah; he lost it all and was misguided.

184
00:12:58,844 --> 00:12:59,284
Why?

185
00:12:59,391 --> 00:13:01,697
Because of his attachment to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), and why?

186
00:13:01,931 --> 00:13:03,171
وَاتَّبَعَ هَوَاهُ ۚ

187
00:13:03,191 --> 00:13:05,423
Because he followed his own desires.

188
00:13:05,838 --> 00:13:08,627
Do not follow desires and do not follow this world.

189
00:13:08,747 --> 00:13:11,174
Because that is contrary to the meaning of the word Islam.

190
00:13:11,194 --> 00:13:14,340
Let's go back to the basics; Islam; what does it mean?

191
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:15,558
Submission to Allah.

192
00:13:15,938 --> 00:13:20,671
You submit to Allah even if it's against to your own will; even if it's against your own desires.

193
00:13:20,898 --> 00:13:24,334
You give up what you want, for the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

194
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:31,886
We want to follow the religion according to our understandings, and according to our convenience, and to our spare time.

195
00:13:32,413 --> 00:13:36,630
No! We do not custom make Islam to serve us.

196
00:13:37,016 --> 00:13:39,870
We change ourselves to fit in Islam.

197
00:13:41,123 --> 00:13:46,819
We do not make Islam change; we change our own characters to fit Islam.

198
00:13:47,045 --> 00:13:52,121
Because this is the meaning of the world Islam; it is complete submission; submission to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

199
00:13:52,621 --> 00:13:56,321
This man; he had the knowledge, and he had the Ayaat(آيات) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, he didn't do him, any good.

200
00:13:56,908 --> 00:13:59,676
Because he was followed his own desires and he was mislead.

201
00:14:02,036 --> 00:14:10,394
قَال صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:إِنَّ مِمَّا أَتَخَوَّفُ عَلَيْكُمْ رَجُلٌ قَرَأَ الْقُرْآنَ حَتَّى إِذَا رُئِيَتْ بَهْجَتُهُ  عَلَى وَجْهِه

202
00:14:11,192 --> 00:14:15,505
 وَعَلَيْهِ رِدْءًا لِلإِسْلامِ اِعْتَرَاهُ إِلَى مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ،

203
00:14:15,865 --> 00:14:21,087
انْسَلَخَ مِنْهُ , وَنَبَذَهُ وَرَاءَ ظَهْرِهِ , وَخَرَجَ عَلَى جَارِهِ بِالسَّيْفِ وَرَمَاهُ بِالشِّرْكِ

204
00:14:21,474 --> 00:14:22,840
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

205
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:32,670
The thing that I fear most on you; is a man who memorizes Qur'an; until the light of Qur'an shows up on his face,

206
00:14:33,316 --> 00:14:37,670
and then he detaches himself from the Ayaat(آيات) of Allah,

207
00:14:39,016 --> 00:14:43,550
and he carries the sword on his neighbour, and he accuses him of Shirk(شرك).

208
00:14:44,735 --> 00:14:47,289
He accuses him, that he's a Mushrik(مشرك); a nonbeliever.

209
00:14:48,175 --> 00:14:49,534
Hadifah bil Yaman(حديفه باليمان) said;

210
00:14:49,734 --> 00:14:53,581
يا رسول الله، أيهما أولى بالشرك، المرمي أم الرامي؟

211
00:14:53,728 --> 00:14:55,457
فقَال صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بل الرامي

212
00:14:58,397 --> 00:15:00,378
Hadifah bil Yaman(حديفه باليمان) asked Rasool Allah ﷺ;

213
00:15:00,418 --> 00:15:02,072
Who is the Mushrik(مشرك) among them.

214
00:15:02,305 --> 00:15:04,208
The accuser or the accused.

215
00:15:04,952 --> 00:15:06,911
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; The accuser.

216
00:15:07,991 --> 00:15:10,584
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says that this is; Asna'd Jaiyid(اسناد جید).

217
00:15:11,444 --> 00:15:15,647
This is a man who has Qur'an in his heart, and Qur'an is showing from his face; the light of Qur'an.

218
00:15:16,053 --> 00:15:18,934
But then, he detached himself from Qur'an.

219
00:15:19,667 --> 00:15:23,592
He fell into the Fitnah(فِتْنَه); a Fitnah(فِتْنَه); and he carried the sword on his neighbour; a Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

220
00:15:24,512 --> 00:15:26,837
And he accuses his neighbour of Shirk(شرك).

221
00:15:27,764 --> 00:15:30,897
So Rasool Allah ﷺ says that, this man; he has became a Mushrik(مشرك).

222
00:15:31,944 --> 00:15:34,516
Qur'an is still in his heart; he became a Mushrik(مشرك).

223
00:15:35,216 --> 00:15:37,969
In another story, and we'll close with this.

224
00:15:38,116 --> 00:15:43,122
Barseesah(برسيسه); the story of Barseesah(برسيسه); this is a man from the children of Israel(اسرائيل),

225
00:15:43,142 --> 00:15:45,729
who was a worshipper; famous worshipper; Abid(عابد).

226
00:15:46,535 --> 00:15:50,901
He had his temple, and he devoted himself to worship in his monastery.

227
00:15:51,281 --> 00:15:56,213
Three men from the children of Israel(اسرائيل) wanted to go out for Jihad(جهاد); Al-Ghazwoo(الغزو).

228
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:57,213
They had a sister.

229
00:15:57,747 --> 00:15:59,819
They didn't know where to leave their sister.

230
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:04,352
So they said; Where should we leave her, we can't leave her alone?

231
00:16:04,566 --> 00:16:05,286
Where should we leave her?

232
00:16:05,312 --> 00:16:06,139
They asked around;

233
00:16:06,159 --> 00:16:09,442
they said the best place to leave her is with that Abid(عابد); that worshiper.

234
00:16:09,489 --> 00:16:14,734
He is the most righteous person; he is the most trustworthy; leave your sister with him; and he will take care of her.

235
00:16:15,268 --> 00:16:18,514
 They went to the Abid(عابد); the worshipper; Barseesah(برسيسه).

236
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:23,967
They told him; this is a situation; we want to go out for Ghazu(غزو), can you please take care of our sister?

237
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:24,567
He said;

238
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:25,487
اَعُوْذُ بِالله مِنْكُمْ

239
00:16:25,513 --> 00:16:27,906
I seek refuge in Allah from you! Stay away from me.

240
00:16:28,666 --> 00:16:30,535
Then Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to him and said;

241
00:16:31,875 --> 00:16:33,684
Who are you going to leave her with?

242
00:16:34,344 --> 00:16:40,157
If you don't take care of her, an evil person may take care of her and then you know what will happen.

243
00:16:41,310 --> 00:16:44,211
How come you going to leave this good slip out of your hands.

244
00:16:46,650 --> 00:16:49,400
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is encouraging him to do good.

245
00:16:50,223 --> 00:16:52,688
So he called them back and said; Okay, I'll take care of her.

246
00:16:53,988 --> 00:16:57,494
She's not going to stay with me in my monastery; she's going to stay in that home over there.

247
00:16:57,528 --> 00:17:00,436
He had a house, he said; You stay there; I stay in my temple.

248
00:17:01,864 --> 00:17:04,225
So she would stay in that house, in the room.

249
00:17:04,952 --> 00:17:12,414
And he would carry the food for her and he would leave the food on his doorstep; he doesn't even want to go to her house.

250
00:17:12,841 --> 00:17:16,874
He would leave it on the doorstep and she would have to come and pick up the food; He does not even want to see her.

251
00:17:17,754 --> 00:17:20,660
And then, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to him and said; What are you doing?

252
00:17:21,407 --> 00:17:26,042
Don't you know that when she walks out from her room and comes to your temple; people can see her.

253
00:17:27,476 --> 00:17:29,796
You have to deliver the food to her doorstep.

254
00:17:31,416 --> 00:17:32,369
He said, yes; that's true.

255
00:17:32,442 --> 00:17:36,229
And Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is not speaking to him face to face, this is waswasa(وسوسه); inspirations.

256
00:17:37,329 --> 00:17:38,133
He said, that's true.

257
00:17:39,179 --> 00:17:43,093
He started taking that food, and he would drop it on her doorstep.

258
00:17:44,293 --> 00:17:48,345
That continue for a while, and then Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) told him;

259
00:17:48,645 --> 00:17:52,791
She's still opening the door and coming out to take the plate, somebody can still see her.

260
00:17:53,138 --> 00:17:55,436
You have to deliver the plate into her own room.

261
00:17:57,027 --> 00:17:59,121
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is telling him to do good things.

262
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:05,999
So he started taking the plate, and he would put it in the room, and then he would leave.

263
00:18:07,619 --> 00:18:10,435
And that continued for a while, and these three brother were late.

264
00:18:10,775 --> 00:18:12,088
This Ghazwa(غزوة) took a while.

265
00:18:12,735 --> 00:18:14,448
So Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to him and said;

266
00:18:14,821 --> 00:18:20,193
You are going to leave her alone, with nobody to take care of her; nobody to speak with;

267
00:18:20,273 --> 00:18:24,869
she is been in there like, she is in prison; speaking to no one.

268
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:32,565
So why don't you take that responsibility, and go and speak with her, and just socialize a little bit to take care of her.

269
00:18:33,025 --> 00:18:36,748
Because she could go out, and find another man, and start having a relation with him.

270
00:18:37,668 --> 00:18:42,152
So he would speak from outside her room, and she would be speaking from in her room,

271
00:18:42,172 --> 00:18:44,943
and they would be screaming at each other to hear each other.

272
00:18:46,549 --> 00:18:49,515
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) told him; Why don't you make it a little bit convenient for yourself?

273
00:18:49,535 --> 00:18:54,389
Instead of screaming and hollering at each other from far distances; why don't you go and sit in the same room?

274
00:18:55,469 --> 00:18:59,648
So he started sitting with her in the same room, spending some time with her,

275
00:18:59,842 --> 00:19:03,415
and then slowly and slowly, they started spending hours together.

276
00:19:03,788 --> 00:19:10,211
And they started getting closer and closer and closer until, the great Abid(عابد) committed Zina(زنا).

277
00:19:11,938 --> 00:19:12,738
She became pregnant.

278
00:19:13,024 --> 00:19:14,134
The story didn't end yet.

279
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:16,700
She became pregnant.

280
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:19,054
She delivered a child.

281
00:19:20,487 --> 00:19:22,617
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to him and said; What have you done?

282
00:19:23,246 --> 00:19:25,503
Do you know what will happen when the brothers come back?

283
00:19:26,736 --> 00:19:27,857
They're going to kill you.

284
00:19:28,430 --> 00:19:30,557
And even if you say, this is not my son;

285
00:19:30,677 --> 00:19:34,767
they're going to say, Even if it's not your son, you're supposed to take care of her; it's your responsibility.

286
00:19:35,477 --> 00:19:36,797
We don't care, who the father is.

287
00:19:37,177 --> 00:19:41,454
We left her to you, You are the person responsible for her.

288
00:19:42,707 --> 00:19:49,691
The only solution for this problem is that you kill; murder the child, and bury him.

289
00:19:51,013 --> 00:19:52,616
Secret after he killed her son.

290
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:56,486
Do you think she will keep that secret?

291
00:19:57,006 --> 00:19:58,406
You're a fool; if you think so.

292
00:19:59,546 --> 00:20:00,693
What should I do?

293
00:20:00,713 --> 00:20:01,737
You should kill her too.

294
00:20:04,079 --> 00:20:08,736
So he killed her, and he buried them both in that room.

295
00:20:10,969 --> 00:20:12,319
The brothers came back.

296
00:20:13,325 --> 00:20:14,959
They came and said; Where is our sister?

297
00:20:16,765 --> 00:20:17,159
He said;

298
00:20:17,319 --> 00:20:19,209
إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعُونَ۝

299
00:20:19,295 --> 00:20:23,788
She became ill, and she died, and she is buried in that place.

300
00:20:24,788 --> 00:20:27,268
And he went and showed them a fictitious grave.

301
00:20:28,962 --> 00:20:29,583
So they said;

302
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:30,803
إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعُونَ۝

303
00:20:30,843 --> 00:20:32,395
They made Dua(دُعَا) for her, and they went home.

304
00:20:33,889 --> 00:20:38,182
At night time, one of the brothers saw a dream.

305
00:20:39,535 --> 00:20:41,098
Who came to him in that dream?

306
00:20:41,542 --> 00:20:42,367
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

307
00:20:43,181 --> 00:20:46,094
He told them; Did you believe Barseesah(برسيسه); did you believe him?

308
00:20:48,634 --> 00:20:49,651
He's lying.

309
00:20:50,158 --> 00:20:54,351
He committed Zina(زنا) with your sister, and then he killed her and her son.

310
00:20:54,538 --> 00:21:01,665
And the evidence to prove that is that; she's not buried in the place he showed you; but she's buried in her room under the rock.

311
00:21:03,718 --> 00:21:06,571
So he woke up, and he told his brothers about the dream.

312
00:21:06,591 --> 00:21:07,909
They said; We saw the same dream.

313
00:21:08,249 --> 00:21:09,373
It must be true.

314
00:21:10,276 --> 00:21:14,196
They went the next day; they dug the fictitious grave; they found nothing.

315
00:21:14,483 --> 00:21:21,936
They went into her room; they uncovered the earth; and they found their sister buried with an infant.

316
00:21:23,723 --> 00:21:26,676
They grabbed Barseesah(برسيسه), and they told him; You're a liar.

317
00:21:26,916 --> 00:21:30,043
This is what you have done and they took him to the king.

318
00:21:30,716 --> 00:21:34,752
While they were dragging him to the king; Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to Barseesah(برسيسه).

319
00:21:35,638 --> 00:21:39,541
But now Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), didn't come in the form of inspiration.

320
00:21:39,937 --> 00:21:41,511
He came in a human form.

321
00:21:42,624 --> 00:21:45,642
He told him; Barseesah(برسيسه)! Do you know who I am?

322
00:21:47,262 --> 00:21:52,331
I am Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ)! I am the one who caused you all of that mess,

323
00:21:53,604 --> 00:21:56,899
and I am the only one who can deliver you out of it.

324
00:21:57,305 --> 00:22:01,139
I am the one who caused it, and I am the one who has the solution for it.

325
00:22:03,579 --> 00:22:05,925
It's up to you; if you want to go and die; that's fine.

326
00:22:06,378 --> 00:22:09,318
If you wants me to save you; I can.

327
00:22:09,951 --> 00:22:12,548
Barseesah(برسيسه) said; Please save me.

328
00:22:12,908 --> 00:22:14,208
He said; Make Sujood(سجود) for me.

329
00:22:17,608 --> 00:22:19,975
Barseesah(برسيسه) make Sujood(سجود) for Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

330
00:22:20,068 --> 00:22:21,361
What did Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) say?

331
00:22:21,748 --> 00:22:25,770
He said; Thank you very much! It was a pleasure meeting you; and he never saw him again.

332
00:22:29,953 --> 00:22:33,086
Barseesah(برسيسه) made Sujood(سجود) for Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

333
00:22:33,473 --> 00:22:38,652
And that was the last thing he did in his life because shortly afterwards, he was executed.

334
00:22:39,765 --> 00:22:42,245
The last thing he did in his life was Sujood(سجود) for Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

335
00:22:43,432 --> 00:22:45,528
Abid(عابد) on the righteous path.

336
00:22:45,758 --> 00:22:51,978
But because he chose to take a turn; even though it was a very, very, very small turn.

337
00:22:52,151 --> 00:22:56,923
In the beginning, it was very insignificant in the name of Muslahah(مصلحة); in the name of the benefit.

338
00:22:57,743 --> 00:22:59,523
In the name of Muslahah(مصلحة), he did it.

339
00:22:59,863 --> 00:23:03,123
And it was a very small diversion that he took.

340
00:23:03,490 --> 00:23:06,561
But look at, where it ended; look at the final destination.

341
00:23:06,942 --> 00:23:09,362
That is the danger of following desire.

342
00:23:09,516 --> 00:23:13,635
Because sometimes we feel confident because of our knowledge, and because of the Qur'an we know,

343
00:23:13,655 --> 00:23:16,281
and because of the Ibadah(عبادة) that we're doing.

344
00:23:16,328 --> 00:23:19,001
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! We should always be afraid on ourselves.

345
00:23:19,421 --> 00:23:21,267
We should never be overconfident.

346
00:23:21,567 --> 00:23:26,440
We should always be worried and that is the Khash'ya(خَشْية) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and that is the true knowledge.

347
00:23:26,467 --> 00:23:28,341
إِنَّمَا يَخْشَى اللَّهَ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ الْعُلَمَاءُ

348
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:31,841
The ones who have the Khash'ya(خَشْية) of Allah; the fear of Allah; are the scholars.

349
00:23:32,247 --> 00:23:34,284
If you are scholar then you have Khash'ya(خَشْية) of Allah

350
00:23:34,324 --> 00:23:38,992
otherwise, it is just memorization of verses in the mind that has no meaning in the actual world.

351
00:23:40,292 --> 00:23:45,199
A side note on this story; What policy was Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) using with Barseesah(برسيسه)?

352
00:23:46,255 --> 00:23:51,215
If Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to Barseesah(برسيسه) from the beginning and told him, make Sujood(سجود) to me;

353
00:23:51,235 --> 00:23:53,691
would Barseesah(برسيسه) have done that?

354
00:23:54,328 --> 00:23:55,347
No he wouldn't.

355
00:23:57,600 --> 00:24:00,582
He took the step by step policy.

356
00:24:02,929 --> 00:24:12,294
Ibn Josie(ابن جوزى) says that, there was a man named, Abdul Ibn Abdul-Raheem(عبدل ابن عبدالرّحيم).

357
00:24:13,681 --> 00:24:17,982
This was in year 280 or 270 Hijri.

358
00:24:19,093 --> 00:24:30,149
Abdul Ibn Abdul-Raheem(عبدل ابن عبدالرّحيم); he was a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) with the Muslim armies that were fighting in the Roman Empire.

359
00:24:31,582 --> 00:24:36,028
And he fought in Jihad(جهاد) for a long time.

360
00:24:38,315 --> 00:24:44,434
And on one of their battles; actually, they were surrounding a Roman fortress.

361
00:24:44,568 --> 00:24:51,184
They were surrounding them and while they were surrounding them; this man saw a woman.

362
00:24:52,790 --> 00:24:53,749
فَفْتُتِنَا بِهَا

363
00:24:53,782 --> 00:24:55,862
It was a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for him.

364
00:24:57,875 --> 00:24:59,902
So he started corresponding with this woman.

365
00:24:59,922 --> 00:25:04,384
This woman is a Roman woman in that city, the Muslims are surrounding them.

366
00:25:05,057 --> 00:25:07,900
What he did is, he started corresponding with her.

367
00:25:09,103 --> 00:25:11,600
And he asked her; How can I get in?

368
00:25:13,397 --> 00:25:18,609
So she told him; Become a Christian, and I'll let you in.

369
00:25:21,056 --> 00:25:22,541
So he became a Christian.

370
00:25:23,968 --> 00:25:30,182
And the next day, suddenly the Muslim saw this man; this Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), he was with them; he's inside with the Romans.

371
00:25:32,457 --> 00:25:34,291
This thing depressed them a lot.

372
00:25:35,304 --> 00:25:40,906
Because this man has fought in Jihad(جهاد) for very long time, and he knew a lot of Qur'an, and he had a lot of knowledge.

373
00:25:40,999 --> 00:25:48,049
And suddenly, now here, he gave up his religion, and he became a Christian to run after that woman.

374
00:25:48,722 --> 00:25:59,645
Ten years passed, and some Muslims who knew that man, they passed next to that Roman village or Fort again.

375
00:26:01,065 --> 00:26:02,138
So they saw him.

376
00:26:03,818 --> 00:26:05,564
And they told him; come with us.

377
00:26:06,278 --> 00:26:09,651
He said; No, I cannot come with you, that's it; I'm settled here.

378
00:26:10,524 --> 00:26:13,603
I'm married, and I have children, and I have business.

379
00:26:13,923 --> 00:26:15,404
I'm already settled here.

380
00:26:15,697 --> 00:26:18,770
He gave up his religion; He was a Christian now, hanging the cross.

381
00:26:21,137 --> 00:26:23,396
So they told him; Where did your Jihad(جهاد) go?

382
00:26:23,443 --> 00:26:24,736
What happened to your Jihad(جهاد)?

383
00:26:24,776 --> 00:26:27,526
What happened to your knowledge; What happened to your Qur'an?

384
00:26:28,429 --> 00:26:30,444
He said; Oh! I forgot all of that.

385
00:26:31,305 --> 00:26:34,899
I forgot all of Qur'an except one verse.

386
00:26:35,672 --> 00:26:42,368
رُّبَمَا يَوَدُّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ كَانُوا مُسْلِمِينَ۝

387
00:26:42,930 --> 00:26:52,030
ذَرْهُمْ يَأْكُلُوا وَيَتَمَتَّعُوا وَيُلْهِهِمُ الْأَمَلُ ۖ فَسَوْففَ يَعْلَمُونَ۝

388
00:26:54,024 --> 00:27:00,229
He said; I have forgot all of Qur'an except one verse, where Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

389
00:27:01,169 --> 00:27:05,056
One day the non believers will desire that they were believers.

390
00:27:06,789 --> 00:27:16,845
So let them eat and enjoy themselves, and let them follow the false hopes and desires; but soon they will know.

391
00:27:18,105 --> 00:27:20,130
He forgot all the Qur'an except this.

392
00:27:21,483 --> 00:27:26,899
He remembers a verse that is telling him that, one day the non believers will desire and wish that they were Muslim.

393
00:27:27,833 --> 00:27:29,026
 And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

394
00:27:29,059 --> 00:27:30,663
ذَرْهُمْ يَأْكُلُوا وَيَتَمَتَّعُوا

395
00:27:30,683 --> 00:27:32,623
Let them eat and let them enjoy themselves.

396
00:27:32,796 --> 00:27:33,401
فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُونَ۝

397
00:27:33,421 --> 00:27:34,521
One day, they will know.

398
00:27:34,668 --> 00:27:36,070
وَيُلْهِهِمُ الْأَمَلُ ۖ

399
00:27:36,523 --> 00:27:38,470
Let the false desires fool them.

400
00:27:38,896 --> 00:27:40,790
But one day, they will realize the truth.

401
00:27:44,210 --> 00:27:49,198
When you diverge; when you diverge from the straight path, this is what happens.

402
00:27:49,338 --> 00:27:54,580
This man; he was a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), and he knew Qur'an, and he memorized a lot of Ayaat(آيات),

403
00:27:54,887 --> 00:27:57,937
and he has a lot of knowledge; but he didn't stick to the straight path.

404
00:27:58,983 --> 00:27:59,850
فَاسْتَقِمْ

405
00:28:00,317 --> 00:28:02,355
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى tells Rasool Allah ﷺ;

406
00:28:02,395 --> 00:28:03,535
فَاسْتَقِمْ

407
00:28:04,355 --> 00:28:07,378
After you received the guidance; follow the straight path.

408
00:28:08,142 --> 00:28:12,002
And one of the companions came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him; Give me an advice.

409
00:28:12,364 --> 00:28:14,591
Oh Rasool Allah ﷺ! Give me the best advice.

410
00:28:14,644 --> 00:28:19,423
Give me an advice that I would not have to ask anybody else for another advice.

411
00:28:19,983 --> 00:28:23,124
I want you to give me one advice that will be sufficient for me.

412
00:28:24,044 --> 00:28:25,304
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

413
00:28:25,511 --> 00:28:28,017
قُلْ آمَنْتُ بِاللهِ، ثُمَّ اسْتَقِمْ

414
00:28:28,671 --> 00:28:32,957
Say; I believe in Allah, and then stay on the straight path.

415
00:28:34,351 --> 00:28:40,378
Because we can say, we believe; we can say that, we're Muslims, but the important thing is to stay on the straight path.

416
00:28:40,911 --> 00:28:45,526
That's where the test is, and that's where a lot of people fail.

417
00:28:46,260 --> 00:28:53,013
They followed the truth for a while; but then the winds of change in this world take them from right to left.

418
00:28:54,573 --> 00:28:56,253
And this is the ending that happened to him.

419
00:28:56,293 --> 00:28:57,115
Why?

420
00:28:57,919 --> 00:29:02,287
He missed As-Sabat(اثّبات); As-Sabat al-Haqq(اثّبات الحَقّ); staying on the straight path.

421
00:29:03,179 --> 00:29:06,752
You slip and you don't know how deep that cliff is.

422
00:29:08,272 --> 00:29:14,375
That is the Khash'ya(خَشْية) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; you know the truth, and you are so worried,

423
00:29:15,355 --> 00:29:18,931
that you're asking Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in Salah(صلوة) 17 times; in Salah(صلوۃ)

424
00:29:18,951 --> 00:29:21,828
إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ۝ ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَاطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ۝

425
00:29:22,074 --> 00:29:28,653
Oh Allah! We seek assistance from You, and we worship nobody except You; so guide us to the straight path.

426
00:29:29,007 --> 00:29:35,028
We keep on asking Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in the fareeza(فريضه) seventeen, times, to keep us on the straight path.

427
00:29:35,326 --> 00:29:37,631
And then in the Nawafil(نَوَافِلْ) we read Al-Fatihah(اَلْفَاتِحه),

428
00:29:37,831 --> 00:29:40,178
why are we repeating this Ayah(آية) again and again;

429
00:29:40,231 --> 00:29:41,621
ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَاطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ۝

430
00:29:41,804 --> 00:29:45,051
Because, it's very important to stay on the straight path.

431
00:29:47,158 --> 00:29:53,774
The third reason of evil ending; evil conclusion of one's life; Su'al Khatimah(سُوءَالْخَاتِمَه) is;

432
00:29:53,794 --> 00:29:55,301
الإصرار على المعاصي

433
00:29:55,601 --> 00:29:58,435
Insistence on sining.

434
00:30:01,301 --> 00:30:03,434
A person might be committing a small sin,

435
00:30:04,961 --> 00:30:09,046
but the Ulama(عُلَمَا) say; that insisting on a small sin makes it a major sin.

436
00:30:09,566 --> 00:30:13,859
When you keep on doing it again and again; it becomes a major sin.

437
00:30:14,633 --> 00:30:24,804
And Adh-Dhahabi(الذهبى); in his book, Al-Kabair(الكبائر); he talks about some of the evil endings.

438
00:30:25,931 --> 00:30:30,612
He said; There was a man who used to be obsessed with chess.

439
00:30:32,613 --> 00:30:34,346
When he was dying; They told him, say;

440
00:30:34,366 --> 00:30:35,990
لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

441
00:30:37,310 --> 00:30:38,626
He couldn't say it.

442
00:30:39,833 --> 00:30:45,109
And then, just before he died; he kept on repeating checkmate, checkmate, checkmate, until he died.

443
00:30:47,336 --> 00:30:49,126
Because he was thinking about chess.

444
00:30:49,295 --> 00:30:53,415
Adh-Dhahabi(الذهبى) mentions another man; they came and told him; say;

445
00:30:53,435 --> 00:30:54,395
لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

446
00:30:54,428 --> 00:30:59,224
He said; Give me the bottle, give me a cup; I want to drink; Khamr(خمر) alcohol!

447
00:31:00,107 --> 00:31:04,402
Because he was addicted to alcohol; That is the thought that came on his mind in the last moment.

448
00:31:05,596 --> 00:31:09,065
Ar-Rabi'ah bin Saburah(الرّبيعه بن صبوره); he says that,

449
00:31:09,345 --> 00:31:17,465
he witnessed the death of a man, who used to work in Ad-Deewan(الدّيوان); an accountant; he's always calculating numbers.

450
00:31:18,342 --> 00:31:20,722
And before he died; they were telling him; say,

451
00:31:20,742 --> 00:31:21,600
لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

452
00:31:21,620 --> 00:31:25,130
He would say; 10, 11, 12, and he was counting numbers until he died.

453
00:31:25,590 --> 00:31:29,462
Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبنِ ألقَيِّم) mentions a story of someone who was dying; they told him say;

454
00:31:29,482 --> 00:31:30,382
لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

455
00:31:30,402 --> 00:31:31,315
He said; I can't!

456
00:31:32,449 --> 00:31:35,914
He didn't have a problem with his tongue; he could speak fluently, but he could not say;

457
00:31:35,934 --> 00:31:36,721
لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

458
00:31:36,841 --> 00:31:40,721
Allah did not give him the Tawfeeq(توفيق); Allah did not allow him to say it.

459
00:31:41,281 --> 00:31:42,857
Because, he did not have a life record of,

460
00:31:42,897 --> 00:31:43,969
لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

461
00:31:44,563 --> 00:31:45,677
Think about it, this way.

462
00:31:45,843 --> 00:31:47,476
Think about Sakrat-ul-Maut(سَكْرَاةُالْمَوت) in this way.

463
00:31:47,810 --> 00:31:50,852
When you go to bed; what are the things you dream about?

464
00:31:52,632 --> 00:31:56,826
Most likely, they're going to be things, you are thinking about consistently during the day.

465
00:31:57,819 --> 00:32:05,873
When you keep on thinking about something; there's a big chance that you could see that thing or dream about it at night.

466
00:32:07,278 --> 00:32:12,093
Also another way to know what's on your mind, is when you wake up in the morning.

467
00:32:12,377 --> 00:32:17,835
As soon as you wake up; what is the first thought that pops up in your mind?

468
00:32:18,217 --> 00:32:20,723
Because death is similar to sleep.

469
00:32:20,810 --> 00:32:21,963
اَلْوَفَاةُ الصُّغْرَى

470
00:32:22,483 --> 00:32:23,337
Sleeping is called;

471
00:32:23,377 --> 00:32:24,182
اَلْوَفَاةُ الصُّغْرَى

472
00:32:24,209 --> 00:32:25,146
The minor death.

473
00:32:26,569 --> 00:32:32,974
So when you're going from sleep to the state of awakening; it is similar to that stage of Sakrat-ul-Maut(سَكْرَاةُالْمَوت).

474
00:32:33,948 --> 00:32:40,818
So that's why, the thoughts that are on one's mind are most likely going to show up in the last moments of one's life.

475
00:32:41,078 --> 00:32:45,574
We always think about it that; I'm going to do whatever I want, I'm going to sin the way I like,

476
00:32:46,100 --> 00:32:48,554
and then before I die; five minutes before I die; I'm going to say;

477
00:32:48,574 --> 00:32:49,340
لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ

478
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:50,507
And I'm guaranteed Jannah(جنة).

479
00:32:50,527 --> 00:32:51,452
It's not that easy.

480
00:32:52,212 --> 00:32:53,452
وَيَمْكُرُونَ وَيَمْكُرُ اللَّهُ ۖ

481
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:55,734
You are making a plan; you are plotting against Allah.

482
00:32:56,407 --> 00:32:57,859
This is a plot against Allah.

483
00:32:57,879 --> 00:33:00,376
When you say this; you are plotting against Allah.

484
00:33:00,396 --> 00:33:00,976
Why?

485
00:33:02,089 --> 00:33:03,975
Because you're telling Allah; I'm not going to worship You.

486
00:33:04,181 --> 00:33:08,995
You are making the intention that you're not going to worship Allah, until the last moment of your life.

487
00:33:09,041 --> 00:33:09,452
What is that?

488
00:33:09,472 --> 00:33:11,274
Isn't that planning against Allah.

489
00:33:12,434 --> 00:33:16,439
I'm going to do what I want now when I'm young; and then I'm going to think about Tawbah(توبة) when I grow old.

490
00:33:17,759 --> 00:33:21,418
 You are planning against Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

491
00:33:21,504 --> 00:33:24,438
Allah is telling you worship me every day and night in your life.

492
00:33:24,524 --> 00:33:25,517
You say; No!

493
00:33:25,911 --> 00:33:33,147
I'm going to try to go around this rule, and sneak around it, and then make Tawbah(توبة) in the end.

494
00:33:33,347 --> 00:33:35,680
I'm going to outsmart Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

495
00:33:36,596 --> 00:33:39,446
وَيَمْكُرُونَ وَيَمْكُرُ اللَّهُ ۖ وَاللَّهُ خَيْرُ الْمَاكِرِينَ۝

496
00:33:39,629 --> 00:33:43,543
They are plotting in Allah's planning; and Allah Is The Best of Planners.

497
00:33:45,423 --> 00:33:51,333
There's one scholar; just a few weeks ago, he mentioned to us a factual story that happened.

498
00:33:51,633 --> 00:33:54,676
They were visiting an old man who was dying.

499
00:33:55,746 --> 00:34:01,388
They came in the house, and when they came in the household;

500
00:34:02,241 --> 00:34:06,884
all of the household; they were listening to loud, Umme Kulthum(امّ كلثوم) music.

501
00:34:07,257 --> 00:34:08,801
Umme Kulthum(امّ كلثوم) is an Arabic singer.

502
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:17,200
The man was in the last moments of his life; and the tape recorder was to the highest volume; listening to the songs of Umme Kulthum(امّ كلثوم).

503
00:34:17,640 --> 00:34:18,973
This Shaikh(شيخ) came in and told them;

504
00:34:19,013 --> 00:34:19,653
اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ

505
00:34:19,700 --> 00:34:23,461
Fear Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; the man is dying, and you're listening to songs.

506
00:34:25,008 --> 00:34:27,954
So they took out that tape, and they put Qur'an instead.

507
00:34:28,614 --> 00:34:33,224
When the old man started hearing Qur'an, he said; turn it off and put Umme Kulthum(امّ كلثوم) back;

508
00:34:33,244 --> 00:34:37,184
because she soothes my heart, and he died.

509
00:34:38,077 --> 00:34:40,241
مَنْ شَبَّ على شَيْءٍ شَابَّ عَلَيْه

510
00:34:41,052 --> 00:34:43,942
When you grow up on something, you're going to die on that thing.

511
00:34:44,745 --> 00:34:49,820
If you grow up doing something most likely, the conclusion of your life will be on that thing you were doing.

512
00:34:51,194 --> 00:34:54,079
Never think that you can outsmart Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

513
00:34:54,113 --> 00:34:55,838
You have to have Khash'ya(خَشْية) of Allah.

514
00:34:56,619 --> 00:35:03,092
The ones who are safe; feel safe and secure of the punishment of Allah are the losers.

515
00:35:03,498 --> 00:35:05,565
لَا يَأْمَنُ مَكْرَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلْقَوْمُ ٱلْخَٰسِرُونَ۝

516
00:35:05,785 --> 00:35:10,598
Only, the losers are the ones who feel secure from the punishment of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

517
00:35:10,638 --> 00:35:14,311
Khash'ya(خَشْية) is an integral quality of the Muslim.

518
00:35:14,751 --> 00:35:18,907
To be a Mo'min(مؤمن) and a believer; you have to have Khash'ya(خَشْية); fear of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in your heart.

519
00:35:20,373 --> 00:35:29,859
The fourth reason of evil endings is; Za'aful Eeman(ضعف الايمان); weak faith; weak Eeman(ايمان).

520
00:35:30,952 --> 00:35:36,821
Sulayman Ibn Abdul Malik(سليمان ابن عبدالملك); Al-Khalifah Al-Amvi(الخليفة الأموي); the Khalifah of the Muslim world.

521
00:35:38,308 --> 00:35:41,530
He visited Makkah(مكه) and Madinah(مَدِينَه).

522
00:35:42,397 --> 00:35:48,229
So he was asking; Is there anyone here, who has met the companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ?

523
00:35:48,262 --> 00:35:49,796
They said; Yes, Abu Hazim(ابو حازم).

524
00:35:50,156 --> 00:35:51,195
He said; Call him.

525
00:35:52,236 --> 00:35:53,758
So they brought Abu Hazim(ابو حازم).

526
00:35:54,545 --> 00:35:56,702
Sulayman Ibn Abdul Malik(سليمان ابن عبدالملك) asked him a question.

527
00:35:58,809 --> 00:36:02,701
He said; How come we dislike death?

528
00:36:04,194 --> 00:36:05,704
How come we don't want to die?

529
00:36:08,091 --> 00:36:08,769
He said;

530
00:36:09,064 --> 00:36:13,254
لإنكم عمرتم الدنيا وخربتم الآخرة،

531
00:36:13,499 --> 00:36:15,974
فتكرهون الخروج من العمران إلى الخراب

532
00:36:17,294 --> 00:36:24,574
He said; Because you have built and established this world, and you have destroyed your Akhirah(آخرة),

533
00:36:24,943 --> 00:36:28,876
so you hate to go from what is established to what is destroyed.

534
00:36:30,162 --> 00:36:34,299
You have built for yourself a good life in this world.

535
00:36:34,848 --> 00:36:40,534
You have established for yourself a good, pleasurable, pleasant life in this world.

536
00:36:40,900 --> 00:36:42,600
And you have destroyed your hereafter.

537
00:36:42,627 --> 00:36:45,680
You didn't do anything for it; You left it; Destroyed.

538
00:36:45,874 --> 00:36:47,167
You didn't build anything.

539
00:36:47,753 --> 00:36:51,321
So you don't want to go from what you have established to what you have destroyed.

540
00:36:52,474 --> 00:36:53,885
Natural consequence.

541
00:36:55,325 --> 00:36:58,784
If you're not preparing for Akhirah(آخرة), why would you want to go there?

542
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:03,251
This is due to Za'aful Eeman(ضعف الايمان) and what is the cause of Za'aful Eeman(ضعف الايمان)?

543
00:37:03,271 --> 00:37:06,429
It is the love of this world; the love of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

544
00:37:07,407 --> 00:37:10,748
When we love this world; we do not want to go to Akhirah(آخرة).

545
00:37:11,087 --> 00:37:18,276
And the love of this world could cause a very, very destructive and dangerous thing in the end of your life.

546
00:37:18,822 --> 00:37:24,701
The scholars have said; If somebody has the love of this world in his heart;

547
00:37:26,021 --> 00:37:29,298
then just before that person's death;

548
00:37:30,138 --> 00:37:37,864
when the person starts realizing that he's going to leave the lovable Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and go to Akhirah(آخرة);

549
00:37:38,917 --> 00:37:42,166
the person would become attached to the thing he loves.

550
00:37:42,513 --> 00:37:49,857
He would become attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), and then that person could start hating Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

551
00:37:49,877 --> 00:37:52,397
because Allah Is The One Who wants to take him away from Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

552
00:37:53,817 --> 00:37:56,197
The Ulema(علماء) say, that can happen to the person in the end of his life.

553
00:37:56,564 --> 00:37:59,404
And they say, if that happens; this is Khulud Fin-Nar(خُلُود فِالنَّار).

554
00:37:59,484 --> 00:38:02,691
This is a eternal punishment in hellfire.

555
00:38:03,420 --> 00:38:09,050
Because you are hating to meet Allah; you dislike meeting Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, so Allah will dislike meeting you.

556
00:38:11,270 --> 00:38:14,630
Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذاِبن جبل); when he was passing away,

557
00:38:16,276 --> 00:38:21,629
he said; Welcome to death! I've been waiting for you for a long time.

558
00:38:22,835 --> 00:38:26,078
I've been waiting for the Promise of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to me.

559
00:38:27,104 --> 00:38:29,944
Welcome to death! He's happy.

560
00:38:30,398 --> 00:38:37,303
And then he said; Oh Death! Don't think that I ever wanted to live in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), because of the love of this world.

561
00:38:38,183 --> 00:38:43,843
The reason why I wanted to live in this world; is to fast in the hot summer days,

562
00:38:44,583 --> 00:38:47,955
and to pray at night in the long cold winter nights.

563
00:38:49,741 --> 00:38:52,976
So as long as now it's time for me to leave; I welcome you.

564
00:38:53,056 --> 00:38:53,749
Take my soul.

565
00:38:54,216 --> 00:38:57,335
He wants to meet Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; so Allah would want to meet him.

566
00:38:58,416 --> 00:39:01,922
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al Bukhari(البخاريْ);

567
00:39:03,558 --> 00:39:08,253
إنه لم يقبض نبي قط حتى يرى مقعده من الجنة ثم يخير

568
00:39:09,253 --> 00:39:12,986
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Bukhari(بخاريْ);

569
00:39:13,993 --> 00:39:22,265
Every prophet, before he dies is shown his place in Paradise, and then he's given the choice to stay in this world or to die.

570
00:39:23,892 --> 00:39:25,385
So the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are given the choice.

571
00:39:27,152 --> 00:39:28,867
This Hadith(حديث) is narrated by Ayesha(عائشه).

572
00:39:29,354 --> 00:39:38,223
She says; Rasool Allah ﷺ has said that every prophet before he passes away; he is shown his place in Paradise,

573
00:39:38,263 --> 00:39:41,135
and then he is given the choice to die or to live.

574
00:39:41,495 --> 00:39:46,162
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ was dying; he had his head on my lap.

575
00:39:47,675 --> 00:39:55,183
And then he fell unconscious, and then he woke up, and he started staring at the sky,

576
00:39:55,557 --> 00:39:56,452
and then he said;

577
00:39:56,472 --> 00:39:57,702
اللَّهُمَّ رَفيقِ الأعلَى

578
00:39:57,722 --> 00:40:01,050
Oh Allah! The highest companion, Oh Allah! The highest companion.

579
00:40:01,542 --> 00:40:04,631
Meaning I want to be with the highest companion, which is who?

580
00:40:05,038 --> 00:40:06,192
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

581
00:40:06,705 --> 00:40:14,135
Ayesha(عائشه) said; I knew that Rasool Allah ﷺ that moment, was being given the choice, and that he was not choosing us.

582
00:40:16,295 --> 00:40:16,954
Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying;

583
00:40:16,974 --> 00:40:18,000
اللَّهُمَّ رَفيقِ الأعلَى

584
00:40:18,034 --> 00:40:19,904
Oh Allah! the highest companion.

585
00:40:20,124 --> 00:40:22,823
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ was given the offer by the angel of death;

586
00:40:22,849 --> 00:40:25,363
he was asking him; Do you want to stay, or do you want to leave?

587
00:40:25,536 --> 00:40:27,774
Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying; I want to be with Allah.

588
00:40:28,236 --> 00:40:30,610
Ayesha(عائشه) said; I knew that he's not choosing us.

589
00:40:31,309 --> 00:40:33,535
And that was the last word Rasool Allah ﷺ said.

590
00:40:34,702 --> 00:40:38,811
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسلیما کثیرا

